ank space to make a true statement?\n\n- $A$ has no inverse\n- $\\text{rank}(A)=n$\n- All columns of $A$ are pivot columns" 13194139535634 true] [17592186358604 1113 #uuid "9e6dddf4-d251-52f4-b350-7dc4454f3ca2" 13194139535634 true] [17592186358604 1145 "The invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{n} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=n=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)={0} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the options separately.\n\n- The following statement is true:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $det(A)=0,$ then $A$ has no inverse.* $\\,✓$  \n\nIndeed,  a matrix $A$ is invertible if and only if $det(A)\\ne 0.$\n\n- The following statement is false:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $det(A)=0,$ then $\\text{rank}(A)=n.$*$\\,\\times $\n\nSince our matrix is not invertible, according to the invertible matrix theorem, it must be $\\text{rank}(A)\\ne n.$\n\n- The following statement is false:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $det(A)=0,$ then all columns of $A$ are pivot columns.*  $\\,\\times $\n\nSince $\\text{rank}(A)\\ne n$, it must be $\\text{dim(Col}(A))<n,$ which means that not all columns of $A$ are pivot columns.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" 13194139535634 true] [17592186358605 1000 #edb/ref 17592186358606 13194139535634 true] [17592186358605 1000 #edb/ref 17592186358607 13194139535634 true] [17592186358605 1000 #edb/ref 17592186358608 13194139535634 true] [17592186358605 1000 #edb/ref 17592186358609 13194139535634 true] [17592186358605 1000 #edb/ref 17592186358610 13194139535634 true] [17592186358605 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535634 true] [17592186358605 1041 "selection" 13194139535634 true] [17592186358605 1104 #edb/ref 17592186358607 13194139535634 true] [17592186358605 1110 #uuid "ebcfa253-7e4f-567f-a5ea-73a04f6b3036" 13194139535634 true] [17592186358606