e following statement is false:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\text{nullity}(A)=0,$ then $A$ is **not** invertible.* $\\,\\times $\n\nBy the invertible matrix theorem, since $\\text{nullity}(A)=0,$ we must have that $A$ is invertible.\n\n- The following statement is true:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\text{nullity}(A)=0,$ then $\\text{rank}(A)=n.$* $\\,✓$ \n\nIndeed, since $A$ is invertible, then according to the invertible matrix theorem, we have $\\text{rank}(A)=\\text{dim(Col}(A))=n.$\n\n- The following statement is true:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\text{nullity}(A)=0,$ then $\\text{Col}(A)={R}^{n}.$* $\\,✓$\n\nIndeed, since $A$ is invertible, then according to the invertible matrix theorem, we have $\\text{Col}(A)={R}^{n}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" 13194139535634 true] [17592186358612 1000 #edb/ref 17592186358613 13194139535634 true] [17592186358612 1000 #edb/ref 17592186358614 13194139535634 true] [17592186358612 1000 #edb/ref 17592186358615 13194139535634 true] [17592186358612 1000 #edb/ref 17592186358616 13194139535634 true] [17592186358612 1000 #edb/ref 17592186358617 13194139535634 true] [17592186358612 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535634 true] [17592186358612 1041 "selection" 13194139535634 true] [17592186358612 1104 #edb/ref 17592186358613 13194139535634 true] [17592186358612 1110 #uuid "e05390a7-764a-52e6-88b2-45c77ecf26a0" 13194139535634 true] [17592186358613 1034 "II and III only" 13194139535634 true] [17592186358613 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535634 true] [17592186358613 1111 #uuid "2b73da8f-593d-59d7-b290-89ab874a96e9" 13194139535634 true] [17592186358614 1034 "I and III only" 13194139535634 true] [17592186358614 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535634 true] [17592186358614 1111 #uuid "f448c6c2-f573-5946-bb8f-22f13bf108e1" 13194139535634 true] [17592186358615 1034 "I only" 13194139535634 true] [17592186358615 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535634 true